Subject: <NOOSPHERE>

Hello everybody..

As part of the research for a book I am writing, I have had to
look into the career of the Russian scientist Vladimir 
Vernadsky (1863-1945). Now this guy was the pioneer of the
science of the biosphere and is much eulogised by many of the
trendy, p.c., 'green', doomsaying, crowd with whom we 
disagree so strongly. However, it seems like a lot of them
have no idea what he truly stood for - get this quote:

"Mankind as a whole is becoming a mighty geological force.
There arises the problem of the reconstruction of the 
biosphere in the interests of a freely thinking humanity as a
single totality. This new state of the biosphere, which we
appraoch without noticing is the noosphere... The noosphere is
a new geological phenomenon on our planet. In it for the first
time man becomes a large-scale geological force. He can and
must rebuild the province of his life by his work and thought,
rebuild it radically in comparision with the past. Wider and
wider creative possibilities open before him."

I suspect this would give most green lefties apoplexy!
Vernadsky was, in reality, a man who could intelligently
balance ecocentrism and technocentrism - his vision of the
noosphere was one where ecology and technology come together
in a conscious synthesis, sustaining a more ordered and
information-rich system. Vernadsky was, in fact, the very 
epitome of an Extropian.

***

On another note: I've only been on this mailing list for a few
days and already my inbasket is being clogged up with a load
of rubbish on such peripheral subjects as "Paganism". Yawn!
Let's get back down to the proper business of being rational
beings shall we. This is the Extropians mailing list - not a
forum for such obvious nonsense as "channelling", 
"the Goddess", or what you get up to with your girlfriend in a 
magic circle.
