Date: Thu, 8 Jul 93 12:00:39 EDT
From: pmetzger@lehman.com (Perry E. Metzger)
Subject: The Extropians FAQ is back from the dead
X-Reposting-Policy: redistribute only with permission

Yes, after years in a bath of liquid nitrogen, technology has advanced
enough that the extropians FAQ is being revived from cryonic
suspension.

And yes, I'm taking ownership of the thing.

The FAQ is currently envisioned as a large living document suitable as
a thorough introduction to a large fraction of the Extropian
philosophy and major topics related to it. It will have sections on
everything that tends to come up, from politics to cryptography. (I
might even have Tim May's full scale analysis of paganism included in
one section if it looks good enough.)

Given the expected size and scope of the document, and the fact that I
want it to be of maximum quality, I'm writing it as a Texinfo
document. For those not in the know, TeXinfo is a format that allows
you to produce, from the same document, either a well structured
hypertext document (viewable in Emacs's Info mode or with a standalone
Info viewer) or a very nicely formatted book produced with TeX.

I've picked TeXinfo largely so that the FAQ will be available in both
of these formats, and because TeXinfo is free software -- the viewers
and all the rest are all available under copyleft.

Admittedly, this decision on format will doubtless be contraversial,
and I myself have vigorously opposed using such formats in the past --
however, the mark of a rational person is the ability to change one's
mind, and I've changed mine. I will likely try producing a Perl script
to turn the FAQ into a linear Ascii document for poor schlubs who
can't read Info documents and who can't handle producing a printed
version.  (The viewer for Info files will run on practically any Unix
box or PC, but there are other platforms out there. Info files are
also pure Ascii text to begin with, but aren't structured in a "nice"
way.)

As to the contents of the FAQ, it is going to be written on the usual
"stone soup" basis. I'm going to provide a skeleton and editorial
services, and probably will contribute some major sections myself, but
I'm going to be relying on help from you, the extropian public, in
filling the thing out. If you are interested in contributing, please
get in touch.

Lastly, I'm going to mention that the thing is likely going to be way,
way too big for standard email distribution, so I'm going to have to
come up with an alternative. I'm thinking that the "right thing" is to
leave it for FTP for those who have FTP and have Harry set up a
mailing list to send periodic diff-based updates to those that don't
have FTP.

Look for version 0.0 of the FAQ to appear sometime late next week!

Perry

who's listed on the Hawthorne Exchange as "P", and who currently has
the highest market valuation of anyone other than the exchange itself.

